{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"eabf6790-d594-49d0-8df3-c9a1b2143b40","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have successfully completed the implementation of `lab-15-dsm`.\n\nHere is a summary of the work:\n1. **Implemented Simulator (`dsm.c`):** Created a C11 user-level Software DSM simulator that uses `mprotect()` and `SIGSEGV` to intercept memory writes, create twins, and generate diffs for a multiple-writer protocol based on Lazy Release Consistency (LRC). It uses `fork()` and `socketpair` to simulate Node A and Node B writing to different parts of the same shared page and merging diffs.\n2. **Setup Build \u0026 Tests:** Added a `Makefile` supporting `all`, `run`, `test` (exits non-zero on failure and prints `PASS`), and `clean`, alongside a `.gitignore` to avoid tracking binaries.\n3. **VM Execution \u0026 Capture:** Executed the lab within the `aos` Lima VM. Generated and successfully captured `expected-output.txt` using the `run-in-vm.sh ... capture` script.\n4. **Updated Documentation (`README.md`):** Populated the `README.md` keeping the seed frontmatter but bumping `status` to `solid`. Added concepts mapped to L07b, run commands, real numeric outputs/timings using `clock_gettime()`, explanation of the multiple-writer coherence protocol and NUMA overheads, 3 experiments, and 3 folded Q\u0026As per the instructions. Confirmed adherence to Vault styling constraints (no emojis, single sentence per line, ASCII punctuation).\n5. **Committed Changes:** Added only the target paths and committed the changes with a conventional commit message.\n6. **Generated Report:** Wrote the short operational report to `/Users/shreejitverma/github/career-ops/library/01-CS-Foundations/Operating-Systems/CS6210-AOS/crew/runner/reports/lab-15-dsm.md`.\n","duration_seconds":153.390383,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":99271,"output_tokens":14815,"thinking_tokens":8046,"cache_read_tokens":680185,"total_tokens":114086}}}
